    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d400">

                <pb facs="0572" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg480"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/2542a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in France</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-07T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6198. United Press received telegram today before 1 p.m. announcing armistice had
                    been signed. Telegram published at once and greatest excitement and enthusiasm
                    prevails. This Department and War Department have been informed no foundation
                    for story. Please find out why censor passed this report as the incident is most
                    unfortunate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
